{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790275659,"nonce":"GSg2FtzjdYjkvIbEZ3Si4jEyCX4=","title":"Macro try/catch: typed catches, Error objects, thrown values","message":"Macros catching typer errors got a String, and every catch clause took every error: `catch (e:haxe.macro.Expr.Error) e.message` failed with \"String has no field 'message'\" (HelperMacros.typeErrorText; Issue3616, 3714, 5322, 7388, TestKeyValueIterator).\n\nNow: `throw v` raises MacroError::Thrown carrying v; a catch is chosen by its type (String/Int/Float/Bool by value kind, Error/Exception for compiler errors, Dynamic/Any/untyped for all); a compiler error is bound as a haxe.macro.Error shaped object {message, pos, childErrors}. The typer-deferral signal stays catchable only by catch-alls (typeError's `catch (e:Dynamic)`), so a typed Error catch lets the call defer and then sees the typer's real error.\n\nThose rows move to WRONG_ANSWER: the typer does not report the errors haxe does (private access, static-through-instance, ...), a typechecker-strictness gap.","files":null}]}